1
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:29,095
If you don't mind, you have a feeling,

2
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:31,287
you're thinking of thinking.

3
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:33,977
You're not a baby!

4
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:42,940
Let's give you a true
feeling, I hope you're who,

5
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:45,060
you hope you're who. Hey!

6
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:48,057
Now that I'm on, it's not a chance to run.

7
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:50,905
I hope you're who you,
you hope you're who you.

8
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:53,797
I hope you're who you,
you hope you're who you.

9
00:00:53,880 --> 00:01:00,457
Thank you

10
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:01,370
so much.

11
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:25,657
I don't want to die until I die.

12
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:29,620
I love you, yes, I love you.

13
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:46,697
Magic is a cutting-edge
field of study in this world,

14
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:48,662
like Revolution's version of IT.

15
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:51,077
It's such a big deal here that a country's

16
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:54,160
political standing depends
on how well they use it.

17
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,200
Note, students,

18
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:02,696
that magic stones like this one are
the foundation of every magic tool.

19
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:07,780
This magic wand, for example, was crafted
with a magic stone at the top. In fact,

20
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:12,720
it was the stones that inspired early
mages to invent the magic tools we use.

21
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:15,317
Today's magic wielders can bring about all

22
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:18,282
sorts of phenomena depending
upon their strength.

23
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:23,342
The greater and purer one's talent is, the
greater the wonders they are capable of.

24
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:29,760
Of course, mining and distribution of
magic stones is nationally regulated.

25
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:31,260
In this nation,

26
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:35,557
they are managed by the Aurousseau Company
with the permission of the royal family.

27
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:38,320
As an aside, that's my Linnaeus household.

28
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:44,400
Now, during today's lesson, practice
firing magic shots with your wands.

29
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:46,876
Your targets will represent monsters.

30
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:48,415
Try to envision them.

31
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:57,298
Wait, there's more!

32
00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:00,737
These stones are the reason there's
monsters running around in the first place.

33
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:02,517
The monsters were normal
animals until they

34
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:04,497
decided to shove the
stones down their gullets.

35
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:06,597
Now they're all buffed up and terrifying!

36
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:11,092
You want to get rid of a monster, you
have to remove and destroy the stone.

37
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:12,090
Right then.

38
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,330
Really, Rey?

39
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:23,057
Every time I look over at
you, you're spacing out.

40
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:24,611
What's going on with you?

41
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:27,920
Oh, nothing really, just
daydreaming. Nothing indeed.

42
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,800
I understand this may be review for you,

43
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:33,557
but even a dual caster
needs to practice every day.

44
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:34,758
Yeah, you're right.

45
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:36,450
Let's see.

46
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:38,427
Sure, I can do a magic shot.

47
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:40,114
Bippity-bubbity-boosh.

48
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:55,592
Wow, I always wonder what was
so great about dual casters.

49
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:58,173
Oh crap, I overshot or overstrengthened?

50
00:03:58,420 --> 00:03:59,880
Why am I like this?

51
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:02,700
I'm officially too OP to function!

52
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:13,495
Getting a bit overconfident, commoner.

53
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:14,410
You're a fool.

54
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:16,997
It doesn't take a dual
caster to pull that off.

55
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:18,437
I don't know what to say.

56
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,037
Your tears of frustration
speak for themselves.

57
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,220
Your tears of awe.

58
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,317
Will you marry me?

59
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:24,230
What?

60
00:04:24,313 --> 00:04:25,143
Where'd that come from?

61
00:04:25,226 --> 00:04:27,040
Ladies, please, don't lose focus.

62
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:29,140
Oh, Professor Torrid.

63
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:33,217
Magic can be fun, but it's a very
dangerous art if used incorrectly.

64
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:35,657
Please be sure to conduct
yourselves with caution.

65
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:36,570
Okay, sorry.

66
00:04:36,653 --> 00:04:37,483
I apologize, sir.

67
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:40,600
May I help you?

68
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,920
I'm so impressed.

69
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:42,977
You may be a noble,

70
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:44,837
but you're still able
to show true respect to

71
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:46,897
someone who's in a position
of authority over you.

72
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,760
A lady after my own heart.

73
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,300
Of course I respect him.

74
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:52,937
Professor Torrid was
one of the pioneers who

75
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:55,837
established the foundations
of magic in this kingdom.

76
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,237
Though his ability is ranked intermediate,

77
00:04:58,320 --> 00:05:01,397
he commands the attributes
of fire, earth, and water,

78
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:04,656
thus making him the kingdom's
one and only Tri-Caster.

79
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,640
I hope this is not news.

80
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,437
Even commoners should know that.

81
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:10,696
Rest assured, this commoner is aware.

82
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:13,057
Our kingdom's magic was quite unimpressive

83
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:15,497
until Professor Torrid
laid down some moves.

84
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:17,286
Oh, hail the mother of magic!

85
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:21,137
Whatever you're doing,
stop it this instant!

86
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,557
You are making a public
spectacle of yourself!

87
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:24,699
I'm not with them.

88
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:36,440
Moving on.

89
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:39,994
It is important to be familiar
with the four attributes.

90
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:44,358
Every elemental attribute has a
different element that it can counter.

91
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:48,077
Earth is strong against wind,

92
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:51,631
wind is strong against water,
fire is strong against earth,

93
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,860
and water is strong against fire.

94
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:57,257
Of course, it doesn't always
work exactly like that.

95
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:58,869
There are some exceptions.

96
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:03,472
Make note, there are other ways in
which the attributes can be categorized.

97
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:08,480
For example, you can use
earth magic to defend.

98
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,577
Walls may be created
out of earth, like this.

99
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:14,500
advanced users can work on a larger scale,

100
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:17,249
crafting walls that
would fortify a castle.

101
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:19,165
Conversely, fire magic attacks

102
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:22,560
and water magic heals.

103
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:26,380
It can be used to treat
injuries and illnesses.

104
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:31,620
However, water can never be used
to bring the dead back to life.

105
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:36,760
Now for our final attribute,
wind magic, which I cannot wield?

106
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,567
is used in supportive roles.

107
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:43,092
Combining wind magic with fire
increases its attack power.

108
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:49,604
While combining it with water
increases its healing capabilities.

109
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:54,540
And end tutorial.

110
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:58,837
All right, if there are no questions,
then let's put this into practice.

111
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,797
If you have a wind attribute, come see me.

112
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:03,233
I will be working with you individually.

113
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:15,040
An earth wall, huh?

114
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,860
Okay, not a big deal.

115
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:35,955
It warms my heart to see how
close you two have become.

116
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:38,060
Prince Rod! Prince you!

117
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:42,317
If you believe I have any kind of
relationship with that ridiculous girl,

118
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:44,257
then I'm afraid you're
gratefully mistaken!

119
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,693
Were you aware of this?

120
00:07:45,780 --> 00:07:48,077
Her hatred keeps things spicy between us.

121
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:49,572
Will you please shut up?

122
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:54,860
Anyway, where's, uh,
Prince Thane? Oh, him?

123
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:57,158
He's over there with Professor Tord.

124
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:04,417
You really destroyed that target earlier.

125
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:05,330
Well done.

126
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:09,717
We've never been great at magic
ourselves, so please forgive us.

127
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,388
We truly admire your skill.

128
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:14,457
Kay, their Highness just
deign to praise you.

129
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:15,775
Are you not grateful?

130
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:17,540
Hmm, I mean, it's nice.

131
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:20,605
But your praise is what
my heart truly desires.

132
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:24,840
And you will never have
it, you imbecile! See?

133
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:26,377
Practically joined at the hip.

134
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,500
Which reminds me,

135
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:31,997
are you two ladies planning to take the
Academy Knights exam together next week?

136
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,180
Come on, Rod.

137
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:36,237
Why would Ray know anything
about the Academy Knights?

138
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,920
Oh, you have a point there.

139
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,517
Well then, allow me to
give you the rundown.

140
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:44,317
The Academy Knights resolve
conflicts between students,

141
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:45,857
kill monsters on the grounds,

142
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:46,857
that kind of thing.

143
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:50,137
They're a self-governed
organization within the Academy.

144
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:54,677
It's deeply rooted in tradition, and only
the elite who pass the exam can join.

145
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:57,197
I think it would be well
worth your while to try.

146
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:59,104
Wow, that's really interesting.

147
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:01,160
I know about the Knights.

148
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:03,417
I mean, they were in the
game, so why wouldn't I?

149
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:07,137
They go by the name Knights, but
it's basically the student council.

150
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:11,037
If you join, you get to see some
exclusive event CGs of the Princes.

151
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:15,002
Which is no big whoop for me, so
I really didn't care if I got in.

152
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,657
You don't seem very enthused right now.

153
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:21,097
I figured you of all people would
jump at the chance to join up.

154
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:22,860
Um, yeah, I don't know.

155
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:26,917
Imagine getting to say, Back Fiend, I'm
the knight who protects Miss Claire!

156
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,860
I can't be Ms. Claire's knight!

157
00:09:31,940 --> 00:09:32,980
It's a villain!

158
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:36,100
Someone please save me! My lady!

159
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:43,480
Are you all right?

160
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,460
I am now.

161
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:47,100
Thank you, my knight.

162
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:52,457
I will not ask what that was all about,
as I'm certain I'll be horrified.

163
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:55,364
But of course I will be
taking the exam as well.

164
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:59,072
And as a knight, I hardly think
I'll need your protection.

165
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,340
Wait, that's even better!

166
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:03,420
Put me down this instant!

167
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:07,091
I won't have someone protecting
me for the rest of my life!

168
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:10,700
Lady or not, I know how to fight.

169
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:12,960
I know that looks!

170
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:14,395
It's your first time!

171
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:15,810
What?

172
00:10:23,420 --> 00:10:25,260
Anyone else feel that shaking?

173
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:33,880
Uh, what is that? An earthquake?

174
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,560
A monster!

175
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:54,697
Take cover.

176
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:58,077
It's a monster attack that
looks like a water slime.

177
00:10:58,160 --> 00:10:59,717
Yeah and a huge one too.

178
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:03,388
If they were to make contact
there's no way we would survive.

179
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:06,277
Get back everyone.

180
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,997
Hurry and find refuge.

181
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,609
While I take care of this.

182
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,297
Move back.

183
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:13,457
Try to stay calm.

184
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:15,140
This way. Almost there.

185
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:31,277
Commoner, this is no time for your danger!

186
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:33,540
We need to get out of here! But wait!

187
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:38,757
Miss Taylor, what do
you think you're doing?

188
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,487
That monster's a water type.

189
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:45,057
We need wind magic to defeat it, and
it's not one of your attributes, is it?

190
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:46,677
I'll manage some other way.

191
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:47,995
Trust me, I can help.

192
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:03,177
How did you manage to construct such
advanced magic walls so quickly?

193
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:05,378
You're not a novice caster, are you?

194
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:06,560
You got it, Pops.

195
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:08,120
I ain't no noob.

196
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:11,037
This is a monster attack
that happens in the game.

197
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:12,137
I knew this was coming,

198
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:15,877
and I have been racking up my
magic skills so I can slay all day.

199
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:19,137
Took a little getting used to,
but it's nothing I can't handle.

200
00:12:19,220 --> 00:12:21,640
Thanks to my sweet, sweet protags, Bex.

201
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:24,637
It's weak enough to
overpower with numbers now.

202
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,597
Tell everyone to turn around and attack.

203
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:27,740
Right, I shall.

204
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:32,571
Students, when I give the signal, I
need everyone to use their attack magic.

205
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:58,512
Be sure to aim through the
cracks between the earth walls?

206
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:01,690
Fire!

207
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,560
You did it! Nice!

208
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:13,980
No, false.

209
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,260
All we did was set a flag.

210
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:26,820
Try to keep your ears covered.

211
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:29,140
Monsters do this to threaten foes.

212
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:33,700
It's called the hateful pride. Damn
it. I can't move. I won't fight.

213
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:35,520
Not good.

214
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:38,057
Even Prince Rod and Prince,
you are immobilized.

215
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:41,140
Are you sure we're not
supposed to let that happen?

216
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:51,055
Oh no, I must have used up
all my magic on those walls!

217
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:06,455
Crap, it's happening!

218
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:09,297
This is about to end up just
like it does in the game!

219
00:14:09,380 --> 00:14:11,337
The whole point of this stupid event is to

220
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:13,657
place the stupid heroine in stupid danger,

221
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:17,034
only for her to be rescued
by one of the stupid princes!

222
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:19,651
Wait a minute, is that what I think it is?

223
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:22,490
No!

224
00:14:22,573 --> 00:14:23,857
I don't want to choose a prince!

225
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:25,469
It'll set a freaking flag!

226
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:28,177
Whoever I pick it'll level
up their affection for me!

227
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:30,237
I need an option that's
not one of the princes,

228
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:34,673
some other name to call, and if I had
my way I know which one it would be!

229
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:36,060
Save me!

230
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:37,680
Miss Claire!

231
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:43,580
That's right, I forgot.

232
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:47,157
Miss Claire's also been caught
by a tentacle in this scene.

233
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:49,560
She shows up in Prince Dane's event CG.

234
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:53,360
It's a super tiny image of
her, but still breathtaking.

235
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:00,140
Miss Claire, no!

236
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:05,000
Could this monster be any more barbaric?

237
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:10,180
That hateful cry was so... hateful.

238
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:13,552
I fear I'm in no condition to be of help.

239
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:15,960
Please stay strong, Claire Francois.

240
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,294
Prince Dane, it's you!

241
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:25,520
I shall support you.

242
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:28,177
Hit that monster with all
the magic at your disposal.

243
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,477
Well, I would, but my attribute is fire,

244
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:33,717
so I don't think it will do
much good against a water type.

245
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:34,720
Yes, it will.

246
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:36,280
I believe in you.

247
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:40,490
All right.

248
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:43,837
Be sure to hit it with full power.

249
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:45,273
Is there any other way?

250
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,197
Not this time! Not this girl!

251
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:59,360
Oh, you caught me off
guard, but never again!

252
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:15,720
Is that an angel I see?

253
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:18,312
Or is that Miss Claire coming to save me?

254
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:24,217
